      "char_start": 46338,
      "char_end": 46395,
      "n_chars": 57,
      "section": "Discussion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Comparison with published incident-AF models}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0080",
      "sha256": "496771903d1235ad807c51c07151a543df611a94568cd15352c27da9b02afdfc",
      "char_start": 46397,
      "char_end": 47251,
      "n_chars": 854,
      "section": "Comparison with published incident-AF models",
      "first_line_excerpt": "These results answer the research question within one health system. BTTN with the clinical term had the highe"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0081",
      "sha256": "51caddfd41ff7709b6f86fcf10d1299a382d5c6b9cfe18b9b4cd8e486d7bc902",
      "char_start": 47253,
      "char_end": 48138,
      "n_chars": 885,
      "section": "Comparison with published incident-AF models",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Published results give context for these values. On the hospital behind MIMIC-IV, a survival-loss CNN reached "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0082",
      "sha256": "f7174e9fa7f1ee408521ff459abd4318b8d3de927685c30b79cff0a9c0ac6fd7",
      "char_start": 48140,
      "char_end": 48961,
      "n_chars": 821,
      "section": "Comparison with published incident-AF models",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The gain of the fused model over the clinical model agrees with reports that ECG and clinical information are "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0083",
      "sha256": "97e89cfadfc082081b474e7bade25aa0cd5a5e9c599c46b039f76ec4e962d420",
      "char_start": 48963,
      "char_end": 49060,
      "n_chars": 97,
      "section": "Comparison with published incident-AF models",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Implications of an ECG term built on readable factors, with a separate clinical term}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0084",
      "sha256": "469e1a4cb2c6fc164b91a067032c1a08bbee4dc9b6d7fccf81169b8ceb8818ff",
      "char_start": 49062,
      "char_end": 50044,
      "n_chars": 982,
      "section": "Implications of an ECG term built on readable factors, with a separate clinical term",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Separating the clinical term from the block-term layer lets the fused model gain discrimination without passin"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0085",
      "sha256": "239b5345c8ba245a5ef5afac98868e60761b4db45e84b5c69228d1a7410e9e78",
      "char_start": 50046,
      "char_end": 51147,
      "n_chars": 1101,
      "section": "Implications of an ECG term built on readable factors, with a separate clinical term",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The PR-window concentration of the occlusion profile is in line with saliency reports of other incident-AF mod"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0086",
      "sha256": "798a82a64c0e43679d397215e2440060cdceb714e43ad42870adbba57d86c9d4",
      "char_start": 51149,
      "char_end": 52121,
      "n_chars": 972,
      "section": "Implications of an ECG term built on readable factors, with a separate clinical term",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The association is not uniform, and the comparison has a limited scope. In a Swedish cohort of 70-year-olds, t"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0087",
      "sha256": "9eaa485136d38fbc17952a423351cb3697cd99c83a39fba0183c63c275ea174d",
      "char_start": 52123,
      "char_end": 52769,
      "n_chars": 646,
      "section": "Implications of an ECG term built on readable factors, with a separate clinical term",
      "first_line_excerpt": "An atrial focus also has a clinical frame. An expert consensus defines atrial cardiomyopathy as structural, ar"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0088",
      "sha256": "d0decde1f4e8cd70496fdbd60b2ab02709d4188d70236a8169f6abe155706000",
      "char_start": 52771,
      "char_end": 52795,
      "n_chars": 24,
      "section": "Implications of an ECG term built on readable factors, with a separate clinical term",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Limitations}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0089",
      "sha256": "461a5eec297e2ce6197efc6b930c559e386d8b91cc5c8af0d47f7319b641d4bd",
      "char_start": 52797,
      "char_end": 53576,
      "n_chars": 779,
      "section": "Limitations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The study used one database from one health system and has no external validation in a cohort with dated outco"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0090",
      "sha256": "a97bf2c6d3b2b402d643d83139da3f453c6504f15f951bce545631155b511ecb",
      "char_start": 53578,
      "char_end": 54139,
      "n_chars": 561,
      "section": "Limitations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The comparator and the covariates have limits of their own. Age is the anchor age of MIMIC-IV, which is not th"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0091",
      "sha256": "4766d64c941baab82b97dece32a14a2a66369783c6ae04071f380bed2605ac6b",
      "char_start": 54141,
      "char_end": 55061,
      "n_chars": 920,
      "section": "Limitations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The evaluation of calibration and operating points has limits as well. The probabilities were recalibrated in "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0092",
      "sha256": "0383c8fb7939c73388d2f0928833fedf8ec91381881478939d0f64f557b1fb04",
      "char_start": 55063,
      "char_end": 55965,
      "n_chars": 902,
      "section": "Limitations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The occlusion readout is a perturbation explanation of the fitted model on 120 high-risk training ECGs. It is "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0093",
      "sha256": "2e0a04b186c2621dce16153cf35aebc08df93ec2598d50a24deecf7cec7e362d",
      "char_start": 55967,
      "char_end": 55995,
      "n_chars": 28,
      "section": "Limitations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Future research}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0094",
      "sha256": "70455db775424f9c0bd78e7309366a6a485be6e5d53cb77cb0dc77d9a594124f",
      "char_start": 55997,
      "char_end": 56985,
      "n_chars": 988,
      "section": "Future research",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Several studies would extend this work. A test of the block factors on ICD-coded labels would measure how far "
    },
