      "sha256": "f141be9c71fcabaeb0b3d88d74caa1167cbbe339178013665d3330de84b68863",
      "char_start": 57009,
      "char_end": 57880,
      "n_chars": 871,
      "section": "Conclusion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "On ICD-coded hospital diagnoses linked to MIMIC-IV-ECG, a block-term tensor network with a separate clinical t"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0097",
      "sha256": "eda5876a1e40f8ebde3c3dc578147d0047bee13bca2e03f1840da4247f8e61da",
      "char_start": 57882,
      "char_end": 58453,
      "n_chars": 571,
      "section": "Conclusion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The ECG term alone reached the discrimination of a compact CNN under the same protocol, while its evidence pas"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0098",
      "sha256": "b185a0dd2bcbebd2282886c63aacb31d37c8a7d4989e1bd4228d1530e0c28eee",
      "char_start": 58455,
      "char_end": 59106,
      "n_chars": 651,
      "section": "Conclusion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "For the design of ECG risk models, the results suggest that a clinical term kept outside the block-term factor"
    },
    {
